            <ArticleTitle>A teenager with mixed connective tissue disease presenting with an acute coronary syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>31-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mixed connective tissue disease (MCTD) manifests as a number of cardiovascular diseases; however, myocardial infarction secondary to coronary artery disease has not been well documented. We present a case of a teenager with MCTD and known cardiac risk factors who developed an acute coronary syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
